1.1.text:
REGENT OF TAMBRAUW

REGENT OF TAMBRAUW

WEST PAPUA PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF TAMBRAUW REGENCY

NUMBER 3 OF 2016

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF TAMBRAUW,

Considering that acts and treatment of violence against women and children constitute actions that violate the rights and dignity of women and children as human beings; that the implementation of prevention and protection for women and children as victims of acts of violence in Tambrauw Regency has not been carried out optimally; that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children From Acts of Violence;

In view of

Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination against Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3668);

Law Number 10 of 1992 concerning Population Development and Prosperous Family Development (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1992 Number 35, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3475);

Law Number 21 of 1999 concerning Ratification of the ILO Convention Concerning Discrimination in Employment and Occupation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1992 Number 57, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3836);

Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

Law Number 56 of 2008 concerning Establishment of Tambrauw Regency in West Papua Province (State Gazette of 2008 Number 193, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4940), as amended by Law Number 14 of 2013 concerning Amendment to Law Number 56 of 2008 Concerning Establishment of Tambrauw Regency in West Papua Province (State Gazette of 2013 Number 85, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 5416);

Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);

Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

Government Regulation Number 38 of 2007 concerning Distribution of Governmental Affairs between the Government, Provincial Regional Government and Regency/Municipal Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 8, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4734);

Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning Formulation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 2036);

With Mutual Consent

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF TAMBRAUW REGENCY

and

REGENT OF TAMBRAUW

HAS DECIDED:

To establish : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE.

Article 2

The implementation and protection of women and children victims of acts of violence is carried out based on the principles of:

Humanity;

Respect for the rights of victims;

Justice and gender equality;

Protection;

Non-discrimination; and

Best interests of victims.

Article 4

Women and children victims of acts of violence receive the following rights: The right to be respected for their dignity as human beings;

The right to health and psychological services from the suffering experienced by victims; The right to legal assistance;

The right to obtain information;

The right to confidential handling;

The right to social rehabilitation;

The right to complaint handling;

The right of victims and their families to obtain facilities in the judicial process; and Guarantee of rights related to status as family members and society.

Article 5

Children victims of acts of violence in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 4, also receive special rights as follows:

The right to survival, growth and development;

The right to basic service needs;

The right to equal protection; and

The right to obtain freedom;

